---
title: Downloading the Final Light Quick Start | Questadon
permalink: /final-light-quickstart/index.html
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
# The one place the filename lives. Re-cut the zip under a new name and this
# is the only line to change - the public URL never moves.
zipUrl: /downloads/final-light-quickstart.zip
---
{# Download gateway for the Final Light Quick Start.

   This page exists to make the download countable. A direct link to the zip
   runs no JavaScript, so GA4 can never see it; landing here first means we can
   fire an event and then hand the browser the file.

   Navigating to a .zip does not replace the page - the browser starts the
   download and leaves this page on screen - so the visitor ends up here
   reading "your download is starting" rather than staring at a blank flash.

   Because this is a real page, UTM tags on the URL work too:
   /final-light-quickstart?utm_source=kickstarter picks up channel attribution
   in GA4 for free. #}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>{{ title }}</title>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  {# Not a page we want in search results - it triggers a download. #}
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
  <link rel="preload" href="/assets/fonts/general-sans-variable.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico">
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg">
  {# Same theme bootstrap as layout.njk, so this page opens in the visitor's
     chosen palette instead of flashing the dark default. #}
  <script>
    (function() {
      var theme = localStorage.getItem('theme');
      if (!theme) {
        theme = window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches ? 'dark' : 'light';
      }
      document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', theme);
    })();
  </script>
  <style>
    @font-face {
      font-family: 'General Sans';
      src: url('/assets/fonts/general-sans-variable.woff2') format('woff2'),
           url('/assets/fonts/general-sans-variable.woff') format('woff');
      font-weight: 200 700;
      font-display: swap;
    }

    /* Palette lifted from styles.css so this standalone page stays on brand. */
    :root {
      --color-bg:    #08100a;
      --color-text:  #f0f0df;
      --color-primary: #ED1E79;
      --color-secondary: #E6FF7C;
    }

    :root[data-theme="light"] {
      --color-bg:    #f6feef;
      --color-text:  #05220c;
      --color-primary: #ED1E79;
      --color-secondary: #266201;
    }

    * { box-sizing: border-box; }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      min-height: 100vh;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      padding: 2rem 1.25rem;
      background: var(--color-bg);
      color: var(--color-text);
      font-family: 'General Sans', system-ui, sans-serif;
      text-align: center;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .gate { max-width: 30rem; }

    .gate__logo {
      width: clamp(160px, 40vw, 260px);
      height: auto;
      margin: 0 auto 2rem;
      display: block;
    }

    .gate__heading {
      font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 2rem);
      font-weight: 600;
      margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    }

    .gate__note {
      margin: 0 0 2rem;
      opacity: 0.85;
    }

    .gate__fallback a {
      color: var(--color-primary);
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    :root[data-theme="light"] .gate__fallback a { color: #A20041; }

    .gate__back {
      display: inline-block;
      margin-top: 2.5rem;
      font-size: 0.9375rem;
      color: var(--color-text);
      opacity: 0.7;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="gate">
    <img class="gate__logo" src="/assets/final-light-logo-web.png" alt="Final Light" width="400" height="200">
    <h1 class="gate__heading">Your download is starting</h1>
    <p class="gate__note">
      <em>Local Anaesthetic</em>, the learn-to-play Quick Start for Final Light.
      It's a 23&nbsp;MB zip, so give it a moment on a slow connection.
    </p>
    <p class="gate__fallback">
      Nothing happening?
      <a href="{{ zipUrl }}" download>Download it directly</a>.
    </p>
    <a class="gate__back" href="/projects/final-light-ttrpg/">&larr; Back to Final Light</a>
  </div>

  <script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-3P5792YKJB"></script>
  <script>
    window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
    function gtag(){ dataLayer.push(arguments); }
    gtag('js', new Date());
    {# Beacon transport so the hit survives the navigation to the zip. #}
    gtag('config', 'G-3P5792YKJB', { transport_type: 'beacon' });

    var fileUrl = "{{ zipUrl }}";

    {# Custom event name rather than GA4's built-in `file_download`, which
       Enhanced Measurement also fires on its own when someone clicks the
       fallback link above. Keeping our own name means the count is exactly
       "times this page handed over the file", with nothing else mixed in. #}
    gtag('event', 'quickstart_download', {
      event_category: 'Download',
      event_label: 'Final Light Quick Start',
      file_name: 'final-light-quickstart.zip'
    });

    var started = false;
    function startDownload() {
      if (started) return;
      started = true;
      {# Navigating to a zip downloads it and leaves this page in place. #}
      window.location.href = fileUrl;
    }

    {# Brief pause to let the beacon leave before the navigation. #}
    setTimeout(startDownload, 500);
  </script>

  <noscript>
    {# No JS means no event, but never block the download over analytics. #}
    <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0;url={{ zipUrl }}">
  </noscript>
</body>
</html>
